    "selectors": "GET or HEAD. catalogue accepts desk. Desks accept source, measure and observation; observation requires measure; measure requires source. Values are case sensitive. Unknown/duplicate query keys return 400; unknown IDs 404; requested period not currently retained 404; retrieval/representation failure 503.",
    "compatibility": "Full desks retain existing fields with additive _meta. Native fields are not standardized observations. This schema validates catalogues, full desks and successful opt-in selected responses; error responses are documented separately by their error codes. Additional fields are allowed. Breaking changes require a new major version.",
    "identity": "Canonical apex JSON URL identifies desk; source selector identifies reader section; measure selector identifies fixed dimensions; observation selector identifies exact source period. IDs never depend on value or array position. These URLs are not permanent observation archives.",
    "missingness": "Zero is observed. Null is never zero. Suppressed requires explicit evidence; otherwise retain missing/unavailable. Retrieval failure is separate, with no observation fabricated. A source may have successful rows and unavailable rows.",
    "times": "Observation period is not publication time. published_at is null when unknown. publisher_updated_at retains dataset/upload meaning, not guaranteed first publication. retrieved_at is the retained attempt time, not response render time. next_expected_update is null unless a publication date is established; cache TTL is not cadence.",
    "revisits": "Weak ETag excludes fetched_at/retrieved_at only, retaining value, period, caveats, publisher version and errors. Compare observation id and version: same id/version unchanged; same id/different version revision or metadata correction; different period newly available observation. Claimant and market-rent observation versions exclude changing row offsets and source acquisition provenance; their content_version excludes acquisition hashes, retained separately in context. Claimant content_version also excludes publisher response-generation clocks. Each rent statistic version covers its own value and definition; a revised median does not revise its unchanged quartiles or bond count. A provenance-only ETag change is not a statistical revision. Official release classification requires publisher evidence. No daily-change staleness rule.",
    "comparison": "Require matching measure definitions, geography, population, units, adjustment and period convention. Unknown adjustment or coverage is a verification gap. Overlapping components and projections must not be added to totals or treated as estimates.",
    "scope": "Described measures: Stats NZ 23 selections, AIHW 40 cells, Wales projection, NISRA 4 BMI aggregates, BoC 4 currencies, Scotland/NI 6 insolvency measures each, England 9 pharmacy measures, thirteen monthly claimant counts in each of five UK/nation desks, and 200 supported market-rent definitions for two city-qualified NZAD suburbs. Only actually reported rent tuples produce observations; known absent tuples return not_reported. Claimants are administrative counts, not seasonally adjusted, not unemployment estimates or rates. All other existing sections remain discoverable with native fields and explicit metadata limitations.",
    "market_rent": "Only the city-qualified NZAD localities Auckland–Avondale and Wellington–Kelburn, five published dwelling categories and bedroom categories 1, 2, 3, 4 and 5+. Weekly NZD rent quartiles describe bonds lodged during one inclusive six-month window. Active bonds are a separate count, not the quartile denominator. These provisional aggregates do not describe current listings, availability or an individual property. Absent tuples are not reported; no zero or suppression is inferred. Locality identifiers are site-owned, not official NZAD codes. Measure IDs are {site-locality-id}.{dwelling-key}.{bedroom-key}.{statistic}; 5-plus denotes five or more bedrooms. One exact inclusive six-month window is retained. A failed locality yields no substitute observation; healthy locality observations remain available with degraded source health. Both healthy localities must report the same window. Cross-field date arithmetic, numeric equality and coverage are checked by the reader and evidence verifier in addition to this structural schema.",
    "citation": "Cite observation id + version + source_url and period/definition; retain the response for historical audit. Row pointer is a locator in that response, not a stable identity. Publication URLs, methodological caveats and licence are retained in context."
  },
  "oneOf": [
    {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/selected"
    },
    {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/desk"
    },
    {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/catalogue"
    }
  ]
}